//! rpcrt4.dll — Remote Procedure Call Runtime
//!
//! Implements the complete RPC runtime for Windows NT 6.1 (Windows 7)
//! that allows inter-process communication using local RPC (ncalrpc),
//! named pipes (ncacn_np), and TCP/IP (ncacn_ip_tcp) protocols.
//!
//! This implementation provides:
//! - Binding management (RpcStringBindingCompose, RpcBindingFromStringBinding, etc.)
//! - Server functions (RpcServerRegisterIf, RpcServerListen, etc.)
//! - Client functions (RpcClientCall, RpcMgmtIsServerListening, etc.)
//! - UUID operations (UuidCreate, UuidToString, UuidFromString, etc.)
//! - Security (RpcBindingSetAuthInfo, RpcImpersonateClient, etc.)
//! - Memory management (RpcStringFree, RpcSmAllocate, RpcSmFree)
//! - Exception handling (RpcExceptionCode, RpcAbnormalTermination)
//! - Protocol sequences (RpcNetworkIsProtseqValid, etc.)
//!
//! Integration with kernel LPC/ALPC subsystem for inter-process communication.
//!
//! Clean-room implementation. Spec source: Windows RPC documentation,
//! "Windows Internals 6th ed." ch. 3, MSDN RPC API reference.

